;; What turns "WireGuard is installed" into "this is a VPN appliance".
;;
;; A box nobody can log into that also does nothing is a brick with good
;; provenance. This pack makes the appliance alive on first boot: it formats
;; its state partition if it is blank, generates a keypair if there is none,
;; brings up wg0, and prints the public key on the console. There are no
;; peers until someone adds one, which is the only part a deployment has to
;; supply.
;;
;; It needs an image with no console login, since printing the key is only
;; safe when nothing else on the console answers, and it requires that from
;; the profile rather than providing it: the getty masks this pack once
;; carried now live in packs/locked with profile:locked.

(pack wireguard-appliance
  (version "0.1.0")
  (doc "First-boot provisioning for a WireGuard appliance with no console login")

  (requires
    (buildroot "2025.02.16"))

  (external "br2-external")

  (provides
    (feature wireguard-appliance)))
